Subject: [PATCH] media: ov13b10: preserve transfer errno and retry chip-ID timeout

Apollo CCI1 master 0 can stall its first register-address write after a warm
boot. Reprobing after a sensor power cycle recreated the stall twice in a
native test. Preserve the adapter's negative errno and retry the read-only
24-bit chip-ID transaction once while the sensor remains powered, after
CCI's timeout recovery. Do not replay mode writes, soft resets, NACKs or
arbitrary reads. Validate the returned chip ID using the existing check.

--- a/drivers/media/i2c/ov13b10.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/ov13b10.c
@@ -769,7 +769,7 @@
 
 	ret = i2c_transfer(client->adapter, msgs, ARRAY_SIZE(msgs));
 	if (ret != ARRAY_SIZE(msgs))
-		return -EIO;
+		return ret < 0 ? ret : -EIO;
 
 	*val = be32_to_cpu(data_be);
 
@@ -1176,6 +1176,13 @@
 
 	ret = ov13b10_read_reg(ov13b, OV13B10_REG_CHIP_ID,
 			       OV13B10_REG_VALUE_24BIT, &val);
+	if (ret == -ETIMEDOUT) {
+		/* CCI has reset the stalled queue; keep the sensor powered. */
+		ret = ov13b10_read_reg(ov13b, OV13B10_REG_CHIP_ID,
+				       OV13B10_REG_VALUE_24BIT, &val);
+		if (!ret)
+			dev_info(ov13b->dev, "recovered chip identification after CCI reset\n");
+	}
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
